  "id": "Compound::DB01326 - Gene::10864",
  "verbalization": "Cefamandole, a broad-spectrum antibiotic, is shown to bind to Slc22a11 and Slc22a8, both of which are involved in the transport of organic anions. These transporters are ultimately linked to Slc22a7 through a series of participations in the Organic Anion Transport pathway. This suggests that Cefamandole may influence Slc22a7 through its interaction with these transporters, potentially modulating the uptake of organic anions. The evidence is further supported by the shared pathway involving Oxytetracycline, which binds to Slc22a7, indicating a possible indirect interaction between Cefamandole and Slc22a7 via these transporters. The integration of these pathways highlights a mechanism where Cefamandole could affect Slc22a7 by altering the activity of its associated transporters, thereby influencing the cellular uptake of organic anions. This mechanism is consistent across multiple paths, reinforcing the notion of a functional link between Cefamandole and Slc22a7.",
